{"id": "unknown-2026-09-16-007", "date": "2026-09-16", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["sustainable_packaging"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "6 CPGs team up on paper flexibles R&D", "content": "<figure><div><img src=\"https://imgproxy.divecdn.com/mVNGu0gugzkQmx4FYLudWdblZmUYpjifcePoxNYhqJM/g:ce/rs:fill:1600:900:1/Z3M6Ly9kaXZlc2l0ZS1zdG9yYWdlL2RpdmVpbWFnZS9mbGV4aWJsZV9maWJlcl9wb3VjaGVzLmpwZw==.webp\"/></div></figure><p>Colgate-Palmolive, Nestl&eacute; and PepsiCo are among the CPGs focusing on small-format, recyclable and biodegradable flexible fiber packaging. Such solutions &ldquo;do not exist today&rdquo; at scale, per the Ellen MacArthur Foundation.</p>", "sources": [{"name": "packaging_dive", "url": "https://www.packagingdive.com/news/cpgs-team-up-on-paper-flexibles-research-development-ellen-macarthur-foundation/830427/", "type": "rss"}]}
